---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import ArchitectureDiagram from "../components/ArchitectureDiagram.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Architecture"
  description="A conceptual AeglysAI authorization architecture distinguishing implemented baselines and offline non-enforcing research from future production control integration."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="02 / Architecture"
    title="Explicit policy. Informed decisions."
    description="A conceptual view of the authorization path and the research extensions that could connect evidence, bounded decisions and continuous feedback."
  />
  <div class="container page-content">
    <ArchitectureDiagram detailed />
    <aside class="notice"><h2>Research completion does not grant enforcement</h2><p>Model D research implementation is complete for its bounded offline experimental scope. The diagram remains a conceptual production architecture, not an implemented adaptive enforcement path. <code>enforcement_authority=NONE</code>; external validation, drift and mock-feedback limitations remain.</p></aside>
    <section
      class="section capability-list"
      aria-label="Architecture capabilities"
    >
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Deterministic Policy</h2>
          <p>
            Role-based authorization and attribute conditions provide explicit
            rules in the implemented baselines. They form the foundation for
            investigating policy-bounded adaptation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Implemented" />
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">02</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Contextual Risk</h2>
          <p>
            Model C uses deterministic contextual risk. This rule-based
            capability is distinct from learned behavioral anomaly detection.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Implemented" />
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Behavioral Intelligence</h2>
          <p>
            Planned investigation of behavioral evidence to help assess abnormal
            or potentially compromised access. No learned behavioral model is
            represented as implemented.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Planned Research" />
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">04</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Policy-Bounded AI</h2>
          <p>
            Proposed AI-derived evidence would operate within deterministic
            policy constraints. The allowed actions, explanations and handling
            of policy/AI disagreement require research specification and
            evaluation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Planned Research" />
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="card-index">05</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Continuous Feedback</h2>
          <p>
            A proposed feedback loop would connect telemetry and observed
            outcomes to subsequent risk assessment. Its stability, usefulness
            and operational costs remain open research questions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <StatusBadge status="Planned Research" />
      </article>
    </section>
    <aside class="notice">
      <h2>A map of the investigation</h2>
      <p>
        The diagram combines existing baseline capabilities with proposed
        research elements. It does not specify deployed services, current
        telemetry coverage or an implemented adaptive decision engine.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
